WEBVTT

00:02.900 --> 00:08.466
How does a bastard, orphan, son of a whore and a scotsman

00:08.466 --> 00:12.766
Dropped in the middle of a forgotten spot in the Carribean

00:12.766 --> 00:15.566
By Providence, impoverished in squalor

00:15.566 --> 00:18.133
Grow up to be a hero and a scholar?

00:18.433 --> 00:21.766
The ten-dollar Founding Father without a father

00:21.766 --> 00:23.866
Got a lot farther

00:23.866 --> 00:25.733
By working a lot harder

00:25.733 --> 00:28.433
By being a lot smarter

00:28.800 --> 00:33.300
By fourteen, they placed him in charge of a trading charter

00:33.566 --> 00:36.433
And every day, while slaves were being slaughtered

00:36.433 --> 00:38.966
And carted away across the waves

00:38.966 --> 00:40.666
He struggled and kept his guard up

00:40.666 --> 00:44.566
Inside, he was longing for something to be a part of

00:44.566 --> 00:48.466
The brother was ready to beg, steal, borrow, or barter

00:48.566 --> 00:51.933
Then a hurricane came, and devastation rained

00:51.933 --> 00:56.133
Our man saw his future drip-dripping down the drain

00:56.166 --> 00:59.500
Put a pencil to his temple and connected it to his brain

00:59.700 --> 01:03.200
And he wrote his first refrain, a testament to his pain

01:03.300 --> 01:07.500
Well, the word got around, they said, "This kid is insane, man."

01:07.500 --> 01:11.233
Took up a collection just to send him to the mainland

01:11.233 --> 01:14.633
Get your education, don't forget from whence you came

01:14.633 --> 01:17.300
And the world is gonna know your name

01:17.300 --> 01:18.833
What's your name, man?

01:18.833 --> 01:21.200
Alexander Hamilton

01:21.966 --> 01:24.633
My name is Alexander Hamilton

01:25.833 --> 01:28.800
And there are a million things I haven't done

01:29.233 --> 01:31.233
But just you wait

01:31.366 --> 01:33.266
Just you wait

01:33.400 --> 01:37.433
When he was ten, his father split, full of it, debt-ridden

01:37.433 --> 01:41.100
Two years later, see Alex and his mother, bed-ridden

01:41.100 --> 01:45.166
Half-dead, sitting in their own sick, the scent thick

01:45.166 --> 01:48.533
And Alex got better, but his mother went quick

01:48.766 --> 01:52.200
Moved in with a cousin, the cousin committed suicide

01:52.200 --> 01:56.100
Left him with nothing but ruined pride, something new inside

01:56.133 --> 01:57.233
A voice saying

01:57.300 --> 01:59.500
Alex, you gotta fend for yourself

01:59.500 --> 02:03.500
He started retreating and reading every treatise on the shelf

02:03.533 --> 02:06.633
There would've been nothing left to do for someone less astute

02:06.633 --> 02:10.266
He would've been dead and destitute, without a cent of restitution

02:10.333 --> 02:14.066
Started working, clerking for his late mother's landlord

02:14.066 --> 02:17.766
Trading sugar cane and rum and other things he can't afford

02:17.833 --> 02:19.666
Scamming

02:19.766 --> 02:21.733
For every book he can get his hands on

02:21.833 --> 02:24.433
Planning for the future, see him now as he stands on

02:24.433 --> 02:26.033
The bow of a ship

02:26.233 --> 02:28.166
Headed for a new land

02:28.266 --> 02:31.766
In New York, you can be a new man

02:31.866 --> 02:35.233
In New York, you can be a new man (Just you wait)

02:35.366 --> 02:38.733
In New York, you can be a new man (Just you wait)

02:38.900 --> 02:42.266
In New York, you can be a new man (Just you wait)

02:42.400 --> 02:44.233
In New York

02:44.333 --> 02:46.100
Just you wait

02:46.200 --> 02:49.033
Alexander Hamilton

02:49.133 --> 02:52.566
We are waiting in the wings for you

02:52.666 --> 02:54.466
You could never back down

02:54.533 --> 02:59.366
You never learned to take your time

03:00.200 --> 03:03.266
Alexander Hamilton

03:03.366 --> 03:06.533
America Sings for you

03:06.900 --> 03:10.166
Do they know what you overcame?

03:10.300 --> 03:13.466
Do they know you rewrote the game?

03:13.566 --> 03:20.066
The world will never be the same

03:21.400 --> 03:25.100
The ship is in the harbor now, see if you can spot him (Just you wait)

03:25.166 --> 03:28.200
Another immigrant coming up from the bottom

03:28.300 --> 03:31.833
His enemies destroyed his rep, and America forgot him

03:31.900 --> 03:33.666
We fought with him

03:33.766 --> 03:35.333
Me, I died for him

03:35.433 --> 03:37.133
Me, I trusted him

03:37.300 --> 03:38.700
Me, I loved him

03:38.866 --> 03:39.733
And me

03:40.233 --> 03:42.833
I'm the damn fool that shot him

03:43.133 --> 03:46.300
There are a million things I haven't done

03:46.366 --> 03:49.066
But just you wait

03:49.400 --> 03:50.700
What's your name, man?

03:50.766 --> 03:53.266
Alexander Hamilton
